### 1.3 Core Performance Metrics Framework
To move away from simple historical row logging, the system calculates advanced operational supply chain equations directly across the combined master fields:

#### A. Inventory Turnover Rate (ITR)
Measures capital liquidity and asset velocity by quantifying how efficiently stock is sold and replenished relative to current holding capacity. A low rate signals working capital trapped in stagnant, slow-moving items:
$$\\text{Inventory Turnover Rate} = \\frac{\\sum \\text{Annualized Units Sold}}{\\text{Current Stock Level}}$$

#### B. Stock-out Risk Alert Flag
A programmable binary threshold rule that isolates fulfillment shortfalls by flagging items the absolute moment their warehouse count drops lower than local safety stock parameters:
$$\\text{Stockout Risk Flag} = \\begin{cases} 1 & \\text{if Current Stock Level} < \\text{Reorder Point} \\\\ 0 & \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}$$

#### C. Algorithmic Pareto ABC Segmentation
Applies the 80/20 Pareto Principle to group stock profiles by economic value based on cumulative financial contribution. This helps procurement teams prioritize high-value stock lines:
*   **Class A (Top 80% of Cumulative Value):** Core strategic revenue drivers requiring strict protection.
*   **Class B (Next 15% of Cumulative Value):** Stable operational items managed under standard schedules.
*   **Class C (Bottom 5% of Cumulative Value):** Long-tail low-priority items suitable for liquidation.

